 gy using examples of key homeostatic processes\, including body fluid dist
 ribution\, blood glucose regulation\, and pH balance\, among others.\n	Out
 line homeostatic control theory including negative feedback control\, rese
 tting of set points\, and feedforward regulation.\n	Describe the significa
 nce of maintaining the stability of the internal environment of the body i
 n the face of changes in the external environment.\n	Describe the signific
 ance of homeostasis in physiology and medicine.\n	Describe the major organ
 s\, organ systems and compartments of the human body.\n	Describe the conce
 pt of homeostasis as the central organizing principle of physiology using 
 examples of key homeostatic processes\, including body fluid distribution\
 , blood glucose regulation\, and pH balance\, among others.\n	Outline home
 ostatic control theory including negative feedback control\, resetting of 
 set points\, and feedforward regulation.\n	Describe the significance of ma
 intaining the stability of the internal environment of the body in the fac
 e of changes in the external environment.\n\nView this event online: https
 ://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198663
