 My Group:\n	Name: EDM\n	Location: KHRA 2-190\n\nObjectives:\n	Define key p
 harmacological terms such as: agonists\, partial agonists\, antagonists\, 
 potency\, affinity and efficacy.\n	Draw hypothetical dose-response curves 
 that illustrate the concept of agonism\, partial agonism\, antagonism\, an
 d affinity.\n	Describe basic mechanisms by which drugs have an effect usin
 g terms like endogenous\, receptor\, and binding.\n	Describe the pharmacol
 ogical basis of concentration-dependent drug binding\, drug affinity\, and
  drug effect.\n	Contrast reversible and irreversible drug binding.\n	Discu
 ss the concept of competitive drug binding.\n	Apply the concepts of agonis
 m\, partial agonism\, antagonism\, affinity\, potency\, and efficacy to cl
 inical settings by comparing the pharmacologic activity of various availab
 le drugs.\n	Define key pharmacological terms such as: agonists\, partial a
 gonists\, antagonists\, potency\, affinity and efficacy.\n	Draw hypothetic
 al dose-response curves that illustrate the concept of agonism\, partial a
 gonism\, antagonism\, and affinity.\n	Describe basic mechanisms by which d
 rugs have an effect using terms like endogenous\, receptor\, and binding.\
 n	Describe the pharmacological basis of concentration-dependent drug bindi
 ng\, drug affinity\, and drug effect.\n	Contrast reversible and irreversib
 le drug binding.\n	Discuss the concept of competitive drug binding.\n	Appl
 y the concepts of agonism\, partial agonism\, antagonism\, affinity\, pote
 ncy\, and efficacy to clinical settings by comparing the pharmacologic act
 ivity of various available drugs.\n\nView this event online: https://calen
 dar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198670
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198670
