 ples.\n	Identify characteristics of drug molecules that determine oral bio
 availability.\n	Explain the impact of oral bioavailability on decisions fo
 r drug delivery including using oral or parenteral routes.\n	Explain the c
 oncept of steady state and the relationship between time to steady state a
 nd half-life.\n	Discuss lipophilicity of drugs with regards to bioavailabi
 lity\, absorption\, distribution and bioavailability.\n	Explain the clinic
 al relevance of absorption\, distribution\, metabolism\, excretion (ADME)\
 , and half-life.\n	Identify common clinical scenarios in which ADME may be
  altered.\n	Make decisions around drug dosing in a clinical scenario utili
 zing ADME principles.\n	Identify characteristics of drug molecules that de
 termine oral bioavailability.\n	Explain the impact of oral bioavailability
  on decisions for drug delivery including using oral or parenteral routes.
 \n	Explain the concept of steady state and the relationship between time t
 o steady state and half-life.\n	Discuss lipophilicity of drugs with regard
 s to bioavailability\, absorption\, distribution and bioavailability.\n\nV
 iew this event online: https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198713
