BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[C3] LECTURE: Review Activity Part 1 - Foundations Exam and Course
  Review and Part 1 of Game!
DTSTART:20261118T170000Z
DTEND:20261118T185000Z
DTSTAMP:20260912T000418Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198807@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:We’re excited for Cascading Health Outcomes\, the game-based
  Foundations Course Review session designed to transition your foundationa
 l knowledge into applied clinical reasoning. This two-part session serves 
 as a critical\, integrated case review for the curriculum\, covering essen
 tial concepts across physiology\, pharmacology\, immunology\, infectious d
 iseases\, and public health. Mastering the synthesis of these domains is c
 rucial for achieving core competencies\, particularly as this content will
  be highly featured on the final examination.\n\nChallenge Structure and L
 ogistics:\nThis review is split into two sessions (AM and PM) utilizing th
 e Kahoot (https://kahoot.com/) platform. To participate\, students must or
 ganize themselves into small teams\, ideally consisting of 3–5 individua
 ls. Each team must use one shared device (phone or tablet) for submitting 
 all answers during the session. It is mandatory that your team uses the ex
 act same team name for both the AM and PM sessions\, as the winner is dete
 rmined by the highest cumulative score across both challenges.\n\nScoring 
 Overview:\nThe assessment utilizes Kahoot’s scoring mechanism\, which re
 wards accuracy and speed\, weighted by the complexity of the question. Que
 stions are allocated points based on the required level of synthesis:\n1x 
 Points: Focus on Foundational Facts\, basic mechanisms (e.g.\, drug mechan
 ism of action)\, and initial assessment priorities.\n2x Points: Require th
 e application of Complex Pathophysiology\, interpretation of detailed clin
 ical findings\, and advanced pharmacology concepts.\n4x Points: Demand com
 prehensive synthesis and application in documentation (e.g.\, complex diag
 nosis or clinical decision-making).\n\nPreparation and Readiness:\nThis ch
 allenge moves beyond simple recall\, requiring you to apply foundational s
 cience principles to complex clinical scenarios .\nStudents should come pr
 epared by:\nSynthesizing Core Concepts: Focusing your study efforts on int
 egrating content\, particularly linking microbiology and pharmacology (Bug
 s and Drugs)\, and understanding how concepts from biochemistry\, physiolo
 gy\, and genetics contribute to disease states.\nReinforcing the CanMEDS R
 oles: Be ready to apply the Medical Expert role in conjunction with the in
 trinsic roles of the Health Advocate and Collaborator\, especially in iden
 tifying and addressing systemic barriers like Social Determinants of Healt
 h .\nBringing Necessary Equipment: Ensure your team has one functional dev
 ice ready to connect to the Kahoot game for participation.\n\nPrizes will 
 be awarded to the top 3 teams\, so be sure to stay for both parts!\n\nCour
 se: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Shereen Hamza (shamza)\n	Roshan Abraham (jra
 braha)\n\nMy Group:\n	Name: EDM\n	Location: 1080 Katz\n\nView this event o
 nline: https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198807
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198807
END:VEVENT
